<vertex eid="3"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered No" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">I01 [NO]
Does the energetic holdout pass the contract?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">I01 | Does the energetic holdout pass the contract?

Status: NO

Method: Hierarchical / cycle and input

Scope / coordinates: I finalist e-kv3-close2; released 0.23 nA holdout; command-only input.

Remaining search space: Complete held-out contract pass versus one or more failed/unavailable required rows.

Binary predicate: The frozen finalist meets every approved contract row on the released 0.23 nA response.

Decision limit: Exact count, 1 mV voltage, 1 ms timing, 0.05 ms phases; repeatability bands are separate.

Recorded observation: Count 26 versus 31; first peak residual 1.15 mV. The loop/trough explanation held at its claimed repeatability resolution, not the full contract.

YES: Carry the frozen finalist into independent transfer qualification.

NO: Retain missing early burst and accommodation as unresolved responses.

Next check: Use the post-trough current/voltage evidence and subsequent reserve result without reusing this input as a fresh holdout.

Unresolved after either answer: An explanatory result on selected rows does not qualify the whole cell.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-i-energetic-result.md

