<vertex eid="6"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered No" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">I02 [NO]
Axonal NaTg x1.5 restores refiring?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">I02 | Axonal NaTg x1.5 restores refiring?

Status: NO

Method: Structural dissection / sodium boundary

Scope / coordinates: g-natg-axon15, sha256 f4a2aa6c24d887343e7003a0a226d6f6d702dfd707e31ad05d44773ea9c5dcbe; 0.19/0.27 nA; command-only; x9; CVode 1e-10; 1500 ms.

Remaining search space: Registered reserve intervention restores refiring while preserving the loop/trough, or it does not.

Binary predicate: Every registered count/refiring/preservation band holds at both inputs.

Decision limit: Cycle 2 &lt;=22 ms and count 15-17 at 0.19; cycle 2 &lt;=12 ms and count 40-43 at 0.27; retained width/peak/trough bands.

Recorded observation: Cycle 2 is 35.068/16.496 ms, counts 14/34. Axon lead increases, but somatic refiring does not meet the bands. FAIL at cap.

YES: Retain a supported sodium-boundary correction.

NO: Exclude this axonal NaTg density change as a sufficient correction.

Next check: Next distinguish residual inward drive from persisting outward load using I03, with paired signed currents and voltage.

Unresolved after either answer: The valid run spent the reserve. Earlier process crashes tested no physiological hypothesis.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-i-reserve/stage-1-decision.json
docs/evidence/h01-i-reserve-result.md

