<vertex eid="9"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Open" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000004"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">I03 [OPEN]
Recovered inward drive is sufficient?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">I03 | Recovered inward drive is sufficient?

Status: OPEN

Method: Impedance / current balance

Scope / coordinates: Model post-trough interval, 6-10 ms after each complete trough, at 0.19/0.27 nA; soma and adjacent axial boundaries.

Remaining search space: Sufficient inward charge in the retained load versus an inward/outward balance that still cannot produce timely threshold crossing.

Binary predicate: With outward load and initialization fixed, a preregistered inward-current replay reaches the specified threshold-time band.

Decision limit: No new numerical limit is invented. Register the replay amplitude/time course and crossing/charge limits from resolved baseline rows before an experiment.

Recorded observation: The reserve does not identify a missing slow state uniquely. Somatic availability, tested Ca_LVA changes and the tested axonal density change narrow only their stated claims.

YES: Dissect which inward boundary or state supplies the effect.

NO: Retain excessive outward/axial load, interactions and other missing dynamics.

Next check: First audit current signs and charge closure over matched V/time windows; formulate a reversible inward-versus-load isolation with fixed complement and a new cap.

Unresolved after either answer: Human voltage does not directly measure individual ionic currents. A model replay is a causal test in the model, not a human current measurement.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-i-reserve-result.md
docs/evidence/h01-i-trough-audit.json
docs/evidence/h01-z-map-i.md

